# docs/sendpin.apk is deliberately NOT ignored. GitHub Pages serves it and the
# installer on the site fetches it from there, so it is a build output that has
# to ship — committed like any other asset in docs/. Rebuild and copy it in
# whenever the extension changes, or the site installs a stale version.

# Raw camera captures land here before being cropped/compressed into docs/.
# Nothing in this folder ever ships — everything that does gets copied into
# docs/ first — so the whole directory stays local, not just today's files.
# (A prior version of this rule named only today's filenames, R0002560*.gif;
# removing that rule without removing the files let them get swept into a
# commit by `git add -A` and pushed to the public repo. Ignoring the folder
# outright, not a filename pattern, is what actually prevents that repeat.)
screenshots/
